        "Content": "Leonard Wilson Keenan \r\n\r\nOur Business is you.\r\n\r\n3/4 Bedroom, 1 Bathroom.\r\n\r\nEnd Of Terrace Family Home \r\n\r\nRichard Todd and LWK Group  are delighted to present No. 8 The Green, St Catherine’s, Rush, Co. Dublin to the property market.\r\n\r\nThis is a well-maintained three-bedroom end-of-terrace semi-detached property ideally positioned within this established residential development, close to an open green area. On arrival, you are presented with a well-maintained property with a stoned front driveway providing ample off-street parking. The property also benefits from a convenient side entrance providing access to the large rear garden.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are greeted by a bright hallway. To the left is the front living room, which overlooks the front driveway and features a feature fireplace, creating a warm and welcoming focal point to the room. From the hallway and living room, you access the large open-plan kitchen and dining area, which offers an abundance of base and eye-level storage together with a kitchen island, making this an ideal space for entertaining and family gatherings. The generous kitchen and dining area opens directly onto the large rear garden with shed, which is further enhanced by the side entrance providing convenient access from the front of the property.\r\n\r\nAlso located on the ground floor is a versatile additional room which can be used as a study or TV room and offers the flexibility to be utilised as a fourth bedroom, subject to the purchaser’s requirements. This additional room provides excellent versatility and could suit a variety of family or working-from-home needs.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three bedrooms comprising two double bedrooms and one single bedroom, together with a family bathroom. The property provides well-proportioned accommodation throughout and offers excellent potential for those looking for a comfortable family home with the added benefit of flexible living space.\r\n\r\nThe location is ideal for those looking to enjoy everything Rush has to offer. St Catherine’s is an established residential area situated close to Rush town centre, with local amenities, shops, cafés, restaurants and community facilities all within easy reach. Rush is a popular coastal town in North County Dublin and is well known for its beautiful sandy beaches, including Rush North Beach and Rush South Beach, providing excellent opportunities for coastal walks, swimming and enjoying the seaside. The neighbouring seaside town of Skerries is also within easy reach and offers a further selection of shops, restaurants, cafés, beaches, harbour walks and leisure facilities.\r\n\r\nThere are a number of schools serving the surrounding area, including St Catherine’s National School, which is located close to the property, while the wider Rush and Lusk area offers further primary and secondary school options. The area is also well served by public transport, with regular bus services operating through Rush and connecting the town with surrounding areas and Dublin. Rush & Lusk railway station provides commuter rail services towards Dublin and Drogheda, making the location particularly attractive to commuters.\r\n\r\nThe property is also conveniently positioned for access to the M1 and M50 motorway network, while Dublin Airport and Swords are readily accessible by car. The combination of its convenient location, proximity to local amenities, schools, beaches, public transport and major road networks makes No. 8 The Green an attractive proposition for a wide range of purchasers.\r\n\r\nNo. 8 The Green would make an ideal home for first-time buyers, families or investors alike. The property benefits from generous living accommodation, ample driveway parking, a large open-plan kitchen and dining area, a spacious rear garden, side access and the added flexibility of a downstairs study, TV room or potential fourth bedroom. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the accommodation, versatility and potential this property has to offer.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
